1. -- { In the introduction I explained the concept of the fortress and in some chapters we have analysed positions which could be considered fortresses. But there are some more that are interesting for the theory. In the following diagrams I will show you positions that do not require much analysis, but that you should be familiar with. In some cases, a fortress is the only way to draw when certain material relations appear on the board; other situations are relatively normal, and you can head for them as a last resort. Observing the fortresses and understanding their logic is enough. Of course, if you are not convinced, you should check their soundness. If you reach an ending like these, with a material disadvantage, you can confidently head for these positions and you will find the right defensive procedure over the board. } 
 *

